---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import {SUPPORT_EMAIL} from '../lib/site';

const sections = [
  {id: 'information', title: 'Information we collect'},
  {id: 'uses', title: 'How we use information'},
  {id: 'sharing', title: 'Public sharing and service providers'},
  {id: 'storage', title: 'Cookies and data on your device'},
  {id: 'analytics', title: 'Click analytics and your choices'},
  {id: 'retention', title: 'Retention and deletion'},
  {id: 'rights', title: 'Your controls and privacy requests'},
  {id: 'security', title: 'Security and international processing'},
  {id: 'children', title: 'Children'},
  {id: 'updates', title: 'Updates and contact'},
];
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Tearleads, LLC handles Command Snippets account data, snippets, public sharing, browser storage and analytics, and how to make a privacy request."
  sections={sections}
>
  <Fragment slot="intro">
    <p class="lede">
      Tearleads, LLC operates Command Snippets. This policy explains how we
      handle information when you use our website, web app and API or contact us.
    </p>
    <p>
      Snippets and tags start private. You choose what to publish. Private
      content is stored and processed to run the service; “private” does not
      mean it is inaccessible to the service operator.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <h2 id="information">1. Information we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Account information.</strong> When you sign in with Google or
      GitHub, we receive a verified email address and use it to find or create
      your account. GitHub also provides a username; for Google we derive an
      initial username from your email address. We store your username,
      account identifiers, account status, sign-in counts and activity dates.
      We do not receive your Google or GitHub password.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your content.</strong> We store snippet subjects and bodies,
      tags, their order and relationships, visibility settings, creation and
      update dates, and saved versions of your data. Copying your own snippets
      records reuse counts and timestamps, which are part of your account data.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Technical information.</strong> Requests to the service expose
      information such as IP addresses, request paths and browser details to
      our hosting provider. Authentication records and administrative audit
      records help us operate and protect accounts. Click analytics are
      described separately below.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Communications.</strong> If you email us, we receive your email
      address and whatever you include in the message and attachments.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="uses">2. How we use information</h2>
  <p>
    We use information to authenticate you, save and synchronize your content,
    provide search, backups and reuse history, display content you make public,
    respond to support requests, investigate failures or abuse, and meet legal
    obligations. We use limited click analytics to understand which parts of
    the website and app are used and to improve them.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not sell personal information or use snippet content for targeted
    advertising. We do not send snippet text to the click analytics collector.
  </p>

  <h2 id="sharing">3. Public sharing and service providers</h2>
  <p>
    A snippet is publicly available when both the snippet and at least one tag
    containing it are public. Public pages can expose your username, public
    tags and snippet content to anyone who visits them. Your reuse history is
    not shown on public pages. Other people can copy public content; making it
    private later cannot recall copies or remove it from someone else's device.
  </p>
  <p>
    Cloudflare hosts our website, application, API and database and processes
    information needed to deliver and secure them. Google or GitHub processes
    your sign-in under its own privacy policy. Our support email provider
    processes messages you send us. Authorized administrators can access account
    information and stored content for support, security and administration.
    CT, our click analytics service, is also operated by Tearleads, LLC and
    hosted on Cloudflare.
  </p>
  <p>
    We may disclose information when reasonably necessary to comply with legal
    requirements, protect people's rights or safety, or investigate misuse.
    Information may also transfer as part of a merger, acquisition or transfer
    of the service, subject to applicable law and notice of material changes.
  </p>

  <h2 id="storage">4. Cookies and data on your device</h2>
  <p>
    Authentication cookies keep you signed in and normally expire after 28
    days unless renewed. Browser storage remembers your account and preferences.
    The app also keeps a local database of snippets, tags and pending edits so
    you can work offline, and caches application files for faster loading.
    Sign-in uses temporary browser storage to complete the authentication flow.
  </p>
  <p>
    Signing out normally removes the signed-in account's local data. If changes
    have not reached the server, the app can keep them on that device for your
    next sign-in or let you discard them. Public-page caches and downloaded
    backup files are separate. Clearing site data removes browser storage, but
    can also destroy unsynchronized edits; it does not delete your server account
    or files you downloaded. Blocking cookies or storage may prevent sign-in or
    offline features from working.
  </p>

  <h2 id="analytics">5. Click analytics and your choices</h2>
  <p>
    CT records click times, element types, the application and environment, and
    public website paths such as /about/. Web app clicks use a generic page
    identifier so usernames and tag names in routes are not collected.
  </p>
  <p>
    The collector also records the IP address and available approximate location,
    such as country, region and city. Click records are retained for up to 90
    days and are available only to authenticated CT administrators. We do not
    send snippet text, form values, link destinations, query strings, account
    identifiers or persistent visitor identifiers with these events. Editable
    fields are excluded from click collection.
  </p>
  <p>
    CT honors the browser's Do Not Track setting. You can also disable CT using
    the <a href="https://github.com/a2f0/ct/blob/main/packages/extension/README.md">CT browser extension</a>{' '}
    in each browser or profile you use. Global Privacy Control does not disable
    this click collection. Opting out of click analytics does not disable the
    authentication and storage needed to use the app.
  </p>

  <h2 id="retention">6. Retention and deletion</h2>
  <p>
    We keep account data and content to provide the service while your account
    remains open. Deleting a snippet or tag hides it from normal use but can
    leave a deletion record and its content on the server for synchronization.
    Restoring a backup creates a new data version and preserves earlier versions;
    it does not erase them. You can delete inactive versions through Data Versions.
  </p>
  <p>
    Contact us to request account deletion or removal of retained content.
    Deactivation or marking an account for deletion is not the same as completed
    erasure. We may retain information needed for security, dispute resolution
    or legal obligations, and copies may remain in recovery backups until those
    backups expire. Administrative audit records can retain usernames after an
    account is removed. Retention depends on the information's purpose and these
    obligations; the specific 90-day limit above applies to CT click records.
  </p>

  <h2 id="rights">7. Your controls and privacy requests</h2>
  <p>
    You can edit or delete snippets and tags, change their visibility, export a
    backup, and manage saved data versions in the app. To request access,
    correction, deletion or help exporting other account information, email{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>. Tell us the account
    username and the request; do not send passwords, authentication tokens or
    sensitive snippet content. We may ask for information to verify that the
    account is yours before acting.
  </p>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, applicable law may also give you rights to
    restrict or object to processing, withdraw consent where processing relies
    on it, appeal a decision about a request, or complain to a privacy regulator.
    Contact us to exercise applicable rights or appeal our response. We will
    respond within the period required by applicable law and will not discriminate
    against you for exercising those rights.
  </p>

  <h2 id="security">8. Security and international processing</h2>
  <p>
    The service uses HTTPS and account access controls. It is not an end-to-end
    encrypted vault, and no storage or transmission system is completely secure.
    Avoid putting passwords, access tokens or other secrets in snippets, and
    protect the devices and identity-provider accounts you use to sign in.
  </p>
  <p>
    Our service providers operate internationally, so information may be
    processed outside the country where you live. Privacy protections can
    differ by country. Contact us with questions about processing locations or
    safeguards applicable to your information.
  </p>

  <h2 id="children">9. Children</h2>
  <p>
    Command Snippets is intended for adults and is not directed to children.
    We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13.
    If you believe a child has provided information, contact us so we can
    investigate and arrange its removal as appropriate.
  </p>

  <h2 id="updates">10. Updates and contact</h2>
  <p>
    We will update the date on this page when this policy changes. For material
    changes, we will provide additional notice through the service or another
    appropriate channel and obtain consent when required by law.
  </p>
  <p>
    The operator responsible for this policy is Tearleads, LLC. Send privacy
    questions or requests to <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.
    Our <a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a> describe the rules for using
    Command Snippets.
  </p>
</Legal>
